  "goodToKnow": "Der Schelm is a rogue, prankster or rascal, today usually affectionate: ein kleiner Schelm, ein schelmisches Lächeln. In the Middle Ages it was a harsh insult. Till Eulenspiegel is the classic German Schelm, and Grimmelshausen's Simplicissimus (1668) is the great German Schelmenroman (picaresque novel). Ein Schelm, wer Böses dabei denkt is an ironic way to hint at a suspicious coincidence. Plural: die Schelme."
